        <p>Aerosol spray paints — including metallic spray paint, glitter spray, zinc-rich sprays, cold galvanizing sprays, automotive aerosols, and industrial protective coatings — are created for convenience and professional-quality results. Yet defects like peeling, dullness, or uneven finish still happen. Understanding the physical chemistry, material science, and mechanical operations behind these defects is critical to ensuring consistent, durable coatings performance.</p>
